  "description": "Canonical US ANSI staggered keyboard layout. Positions are key CENTERS in unit-pitch coordinates. One unit = one key pitch (~19.05 mm on a full-size keyboard, ~17-19 mm on most laptops). The origin (0,0) is the top-left of the `~` key. The homography pipeline (cybertyping/perception/homography.py) maps these to image pixels via at least 4 anchor-key detections. Stagger offsets follow ANSI: QWERTY row +0.5u, ASDF row +0.75u, ZXCV row +1.25u relative to the digit row.",
  "units": {
    "x": "key_pitch",
    "y": "row_pitch"
  },
  "comment_on_y_axis": "y grows DOWNWARD (image-like), so row 0 is the top of the keyboard.",
